From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:20:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015-d221: Hold the Wi-Fi module's UART

On the iPhone X the ADT's "wlan" node, the platform-control function of
the BCM4357 (compatible wlan-pcie-uart,bcm4357, module-instance
herculesk), sits below uart4, with function-tx on AP GPIO 215 and
function-rts on AP GPIO 217. The iPads whose PCIe Wi-Fi comes up (A9
iPad 5, A10 iPad 6 and 7) hold the same UART of theirs through the
apple,t8010-wlan-uart-provider platform control: it muxes those two
pins, keeps the UART's power domain on and resets the block before
pci-pwrctrl powers the endpoint. The D221 had none of it, and its
firmware stops early in its init without writing the shared area
(FW failed to initialize).

Describe uart4's platform control in the SoC file, disabled, and enable
it on the D221 with its pins, linked from the Wi-Fi endpoint.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts | 15 +++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi     | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
index a799db51d..d005a1c7d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015-d221.dts
@@ -17,4 +17,19 @@ / {
 &wifi0 {
 	compatible = "apple,d221-bcm4357-wifi", "pci14e4,440a";
 	brcm,board-type = "apple,herculesk";
+	apple,wlan-uart = <&wlan_uart4>;
+};
+
+&pinctrl_ap {
+	/* ADT uart4 function-tx and function-rts */
+	wlan_uart4_pins: wlan-uart4-pins {
+		pinmux = <APPLE_PINMUX(215, 1)>,
+			 <APPLE_PINMUX(217, 1)>;
+	};
+};
+
+&wlan_uart4 {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&wlan_uart4_pins>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	status = "okay";
 };
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
index 85c1ba5f3..7edfb8590 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
@@ -348,6 +348,17 @@ serial0: serial@22e600000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * uart4 carries the ADT's "wlan" node (wlan-pcie-uart,bcm4357):
+		 * the platform-control function of the PCIe Wi-Fi module.
+		 */
+		wlan_uart4: wlan-platform-control@22e610000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8010-wlan-uart-provider";
+			reg = <0x2 0x2e610000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_uart4>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		bus@230000000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8015-usb-complex", "simple-pm-bus";
 			#address-cells = <2>;
